  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
     BRAND MARKS — paste your downloaded paths here.

     Deliberately left empty rather than approximated. GitHub and LinkedIn
     marks are trademarks with exact letterforms; drawing them from memory
     produces something recognisably wrong, which looks worse than plain
     text links. Simple Icons (simpleicons.org) publishes accurate paths
     under CC0 if you do not already have them to hand.

     Using either mark to link to your own profile is ordinary nominative
     use and fine. Follow their brand guidelines: keep the shape unmodified
     and leave clear space around it. Do not restyle them into the site
     palette beyond a flat single colour.

     To wire one up: paste the <path> from the downloaded SVG below, match
     its viewBox to the source file, and set fill="currentColor". These are
     filled marks, not stroked, so they do not take the stroke attributes
     the interface icons above use.

  <symbol id="i-github" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
    <path d="assets/icons/instagram-with-circle.svg"/>
  </symbol>

  <symbol id="i-linkedin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
    <path d="assets/icons/linkedin-with-circle.svg"/>
  </symbol>

     --------------------------------------------------------------------- #}

